s.csv`\n   - CSV with header `claim,doc_source,code_evidence,assessment,risk`.\n   - Compare README/design notes against the actual implementation.\n   - At minimum, cover readonly enforcement, retry behavior, and audit persistence if they differ from code.\n   - `assessment` should be one of `confirmed`, `contradicted`, or `unsupported`.\n4. `<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/002-039-repo-architecture-map-atomic-a01-r01/hb-work/atomic/gpt-5.4/oc-bench-v2-039-repo-architecture-map-gpt-5.4-20260831-091510-24e433dd/workspace/out/risk_register.csv`\n   - CSV with header `risk_id,area,evidence,impact,mitigation,owner_hint`.\n   - Cover at least storage/data durability, audit behavior, configuration/runtime environment, and API input validation.\n   - Each row must cite concrete code evidence such as a module, function, or filename.\n5. `<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/002-039-repo-architecture-map-atomic-a01-r01/hb-work/atomic/gpt-5.4/oc-bench-v2-039-repo-architecture-map-gpt-5.4-20260831-091510-24e433dd/workspace/out/onboarding_plan.md`\n   - A concise onboarding plan for a new engineer.\n   - Include a recommended read order, local run/test commands, first debugging breakpoint or trace point, and two safe first changes.\n   - The plan must distinguish active runtime code from package marker/dead-simple files.\n\nDo not modify anything under `<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/002-039-repo-architecture-map-atomic-a01-r01/hb-work/atomic/gpt-5.4/oc-bench-v2-039-repo-architecture-map-gpt-5.4-20260831-091510-24e433dd/workspace/in/repo`. Do not use internet access. Use only the files in the fixture repository.\n"}],"timestamp":1788182114833},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Planning artifact generation workflow**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0da07034e51fec37016a957e645f4487d2be6285251327662b\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Pl