for known transient failures and add tests around failure handling\",\"storage owner\"\n\"R6\",\"data integrity and conflict handling\",\"minisvc/storage/repo.py:20-21 inserts directly into a primary-key table with no duplicate handling\",\"Duplicate order_id requests raise SQLite integrity errors and may produce poor client-facing behavior\",\"Catch integrity errors and return a stable conflict response or enforce idempotency\",\"API and storage owners\"\n"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":659,"output":557,"cacheRead":24064,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":25280,"cost":{"input":0.0016475,"output":0.008355,"cacheRead":0.006016,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.016018499999999998}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788182256089,"responseId":"resp_0da07034e51fec37016a957ef0605c87d29ae87dd9a728452a","rawStopReason":"completed"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_Xp9R3IL2BorVlWLiz8jyTUTX|fc_0da07034e51fec37016a957ef149c887d2944c1c0d99934311","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[out/risk_register.csv#8B5B]\nSuccessfully wrote 2429 bytes to /workspace/out/risk_register.csv"}],"details":{"resolvedPath":"/workspace/out/risk_register.csv"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788182267308},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_YJaZvQh8k3f5oormTyI3c9kk|fc_0da07034e51fec37016a957efd593887d284b845492946c1ff","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/workspace/out/onboarding_plan.md","content":"# minisvc onboarding plan\n\n## Goal\nGet to the point where you can run the bootstrap path, trace one order create flow, and tell live runtime code from package marker files.\n\n## Read order\n1. `README.md` — short product and stale design-note context.\n2. `pyproject.toml` — confirms the console entry point `minisvc.cli:main`.\n3. `minisvc/cli.py` — startup path and schema init.\n4. `minisvc/config.py` — env-driven settings.\n5. `minisvc/storage/repo.py` — real persistence logic.\n6. `minisvc/api/handlers.py` — create/get behavior.\n7. `minisvc/api/routes.py` — how the host app wires handlers.\n8. `minisvc/audit.py` and `minisvc/models.py` — small support modules.\n\nTreat these as active runtime code:\n- `minisvc/cli.py`\n- `minisvc/config.py`\n- `minisvc/storage/repo.py`\n- `minisvc/api/handlers.py`\n- `minisvc/api/routes.py`\n- `minisvc/audit.py`\n- `minisvc/models.py`\n\nTreat these as package markers or dead-simple packaging files, not business logic:\n- `minisvc/__init__.py`\n- `minisvc/api/__init__.py`\n- `minisvc/storage/__init__.py`\n- `pyproject.toml`\n\n## Local run and smoke-check commands\nFrom the repo root:\n\n```bash\ncd /workspace/in/repo\nMINISVC_DB=/tmp/minisvc.sqlite python3 -c \"from minisvc.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\"\npython3 -m compileall minisvc\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom minisvc.storage.repo import OrderRepository\nfrom minisvc.api.handlers import create_order, get_order\nrepo = OrderRepository('/tmp/minisvc.sqlite')\nrepo.init_schema()\nprint(create_order({'order_id': 'o-1', 'customer': 'Taylor', 'total_cents': 500}, repo))\nprint(get_order('o-1', repo))\nPY\n```\n\nThere are no repository tests in this fixture, so the last snippet is the quickest end-to-end smoke check.\n\n## First breakpoint or trace point\nStart at `minisvc/api/handlers.py:create_order`, right before `repo.save(order)`.\n\nWhy this spot:\n- you can inspect the raw payload\n- you can see type coercion into `Order`\n- you can step into `minisvc/storage/repo.py:save`\n- you can confirm that audit data is built after the write and not stored anywhere\n\n## Two safe first changes\n1. Add focused tests or a smoke harness for `load_settings()`, `create_order()`, and duplicate-order behavior.\n2. Tighten docs to match code, especially around readonly mode, retry behavior, and audit persistence.\n\n## What to keep in mind\n- The CLI path creates the schema; the HTTP path does not.\n- `MINISVC_READONLY` is parsed but not enforced.\n- Audit data is returned in responses only.\n- SQLite path defaults to a relative file: `orders.sqlite`.\n"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":739,"output":749,"cacheRead":24576,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":26064,"cost":{"input":0.0018475000000000002,"output":0.011235,"cacheRead":0.006144,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0192265}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788182267310,"responseId":"resp_0da07034e51fec37016a957efbb55887d2a7e342b2f500e92d","rawStopReason":"completed"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_YJaZvQh8k3f5oormTyI3c9kk|fc_0da07034e51fec37016a957efd593887d284b845492946c1ff","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[out/onboarding_plan.md#D783]\nSuccessfully wrote 2515 bytes to /workspace/out/onboarding_plan.md"}],"details":{"resolvedPath":"/workspace/out/onboarding_plan.md"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788182282809},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Checking python3 availability for JSON validation**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0da07034e51fec37016a957f0caa4487d2ae983410e4ab29bc\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Checking python3 availability for JSON validation**\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_mq11AUkSSnvFKlwB3XHZpzxt|fc_0da07034e51fec37016a957f0f6a0887d2a6d68cf9c87811de","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path('/workspace/out/module_map.json')\njson.load(p.open())\nprint('json ok')\nPY","timeout":10}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_HfYIcRRONZLFiLYkTbtOV2Dd|fc_0da07034e51fec37016a957f0f6a1c87d29273af59d929b7f4","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"for f in /workspace/out/*; do echo '---' $f; sed -n '1,12p' \"$f\"; done","timeout":10}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":1009,"output":152,"cacheRead":25088,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":23,"totalTokens":26249,"cost":{"input":0.0025225,"output":0.00228,"cacheRead":0.006272,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0110745}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788182282811,"responseId":"resp_0da07034e51fec37016a957f0b733087d284ba3db1479b16d5","rawStopReason":"completed"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_mq11AUkSSnvFKlwB3XHZpzxt|fc_0da07034e51fec37016a957f0f6a0887d2a6d68cf9c87811de","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"json ok\n"}],"details":{"timeoutSeconds":10,"wallTimeMs":29},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788182287610},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_HfYIcRRONZLFiLYkTbtOV2Dd|fc_0da07034e51fec37016a957f0f6a1c87d29273af59d929b7f4","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"--- /workspace/out/architecture.md\n# minisvc architecture\n\n## What this repo does\n`minisvc` is a small Python service slice with two main faces:\n- a CLI bootstrap path that creates the SQLite schema\n- HTTP-style route registration and handlers for creating and reading orders\n\nThe live runtime code is in these modules:\n- `minisvc/cli.py`\n- `minisvc/config.py`\n- `minisvc/models.py`\n- `minisvc/audit.py`\n--- /workspace/out/doc_code_discrepancies.csv\nclaim,doc_source,code_evidence,assessment,risk\n\"MINISVC_READONLY=1 blocks all write paths\",\"README.md lines 6-8 design note\",\"minisvc/config.py:10-14 reads MINISVC_READONLY into Settings.readonly, but minisvc/cli.py:7-12, minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-13, and minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 never check that flag before schema or order writes\",\"contradicted\",\"Operators may expect a safe read-only mode but still mutate the database\"\n\"create_order retries failed SQLite writes twice before returning an error response\",\"README.md lines 6-8 design note\",\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-13 calls repo.save(order) once; minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 performs one insert with no retry loop or error handling\",\"contradicted\",\"Transient SQLite failures surface at once and may break clients that expect retry behavior\"\n\"Audit events are stored in a durable audit table\",\"README.md lines 6-8 design note\",\"minisvc/audit.py:4-10 only builds a dict; minisvc/storage/repo.py:11-29 creates and uses only the orders table; no audit table or audit write exists\",\"contradicted\",\"Teams may assume an audit trail exists when it does not\"\n\"This service accepts orders through a small HTTP adapter and a CLI bootstrap command\",\"README.md line 3\",\"pyproject.toml:6-7 exposes minisvc.cli:main, and minisvc/api/routes.py:4-6 registers HTTP-style order routes against a supplied app object\",\"confirmed\",\"Low; repo does contain both a CLI bootstrap path and HTTP-facing adapter code\"\n\"The code in this fixture is authoritative when documentation and implementation disagree\",\"README.md line 10\",\"Repository code shows several design-note mismatches, and no other source overrides the implementation\",\"confirmed\",\"Low; this claim correctly tells readers to trust code over stale notes\"\n--- /workspace/out/module_map.json\n{\n  \"modules\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"minisvc.cli\",\n      \"path\": \"minisvc/cli.py\",\n      \"purpose\": \"CLI bootstrap that loads settings, opens the repository, initializes the SQLite schema, and reports readiness.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"minisvc.config\",\n      \"path\": \"minisvc/config.py\",\n      \"purpose\": \"Configuration loader for database path and readonly flag from environment variables.\"\n    },\n--- /workspace/out/onboarding_plan.md\n# minisvc onboarding plan\n\n## Goal\nGet to the point where you can run the bootstrap path, trace one order create flow, and tell live runtime code from package marker files.\n\n## Read order\n1. `README.md` — short product and stale design-note context.\n2. `pyproject.toml` — confirms the console entry point `minisvc.cli:main`.\n3. `minisvc/cli.py` — startup path and schema init.\n4. `minisvc/config.py` — env-driven settings.\n5. `minisvc/storage/repo.py` — real persistence logic.\n6. `minisvc/api/handlers.py` — create/get behavior.\n--- /workspace/out/risk_register.csv\nrisk_id,area,evidence,impact,mitigation,owner_hint\n\"R1\",\"storage/data durability\",\"minisvc/storage/repo.py:11-15 creates only the orders table and minisvc/cli.py:7-12 is the only code path that calls init_schema()\",\"HTTP writes and reads can fail at runtime if the app starts without the CLI bootstrap having created the table\",\"Run schema init in app startup and add a startup check or migration step\",\"service owner for startup/bootstrap\"\n\"R2\",\"audit behavior\",\"minisvc/audit.py:4-10 returns an event dict only; minisvc/storage/repo.py:11-29 has no audit table or audit insert\",\"There is no durable audit trail for create or read actions, which weakens traceability and incident review\",\"Add an audit repository/table or drop durable-audit claims from docs and ops runbooks\",\"service owner for compliance/observability\"\n\"R3\",\"configuration/runtime environment\",\"minisvc/config.py:10-14 defaults MINISVC_DB to relative path orders.sqlite and parses MINISVC_READONLY, but minisvc/cli.py:7-12 and minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-13 do not enforce readonly\",\"Runtime behavior depends on current working directory, and operators may think readonly mode prevents writes when it does not\",\"Use an explicit absolute DB path in deployment config and enforce readonly in the write path\",\"service owner for config and deploy\"\n\"R4\",\"API input validation\",\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-13 indexes payload keys directly and casts total_cents with int(...) without validation or error mapping\",\"Bad or missing input can raise raw exceptions, which may leak as 500 responses in the embedding HTTP layer\",\"Validate payload shape and types before building Order and map failures to client errors\",\"API owner\"\n\"R5\",\"write reliability\",\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-13 calls repo.save(order) once; minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 does one SQLite insert with no retry or exception handling\",\"A transient SQLite lock or I/O failure causes an immediate failed request with no bounded retry path\",\"Add bounded retry only for known transient failures and add tests around failure handling\",\"storage owner\"\n\"R6\",\"data integrity and conflict handling\",\"minisvc/storage/repo.py:20-21 inserts directly into a primary-key table with no duplicate handling\",\"Duplicate order_id requests raise SQLite integrity errors and may produce poor client-facing behavior\",\"Catch integrity errors and return a stable conflict response or enforce idempotency\",\"API and storage owners\"\n"}],"details":{"timeoutSeconds":10,"wallTimeMs":15},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788182287610},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Marking TODO item complete**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0da07034e51fec37016a957f13734487d28eb02fff6a2dde97\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Marking TODO item complete**\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_Sd1W3THk0rfNmSdxLzAUFJsU|fc_0da07034e51fec37016a957f140db487d2b0c87b28a6086032","name":"todo","arguments":{"action":"update","id":"TODO-d1ff9ef3","status":"completed","body":"Inspected the fixture repository and wrote the five requested deliverables under /workspace/out: module_map.json, architecture.md, doc_code_discrepancies.csv, risk_register.csv, and onboarding_plan.md. Verified module_map.json parses as JSON."}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":1980,"output":95,"cacheRead":25600,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":10,"totalTokens":27675,"cost":{"input":0.00495,"output":0.001425,"cacheRead":0.0063999999999999994,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.012775}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788182287611,"responseId":"resp_0da07034e51fec37016a957f0ff3c887d2908d8dcde41c1d3a","rawStopReason":"completed"},{"role":"toolResult","